- The body is INSTRUCTIONS EXECUTED BY AN LLM, not code. Ambiguity, missing preconditions, or an
  unstated failure path become runtime misbehaviour by the agent, not a compiler error.
- Bundled scripts in the skill dir are invoked BY that agent, from a shell, with model-chosen
  arguments. So their CLI contract, input validation, and failure modes are part of the skill's
  safety surface.

